**Status filtering — O(5n) instead of O(n)**

Appears in `view.js:116`, `inline-dom.js:148`, `markdown-block.js:60`:

```js
// CURRENT — scans full task array 5 times
for (const status of STATUSES) {
  const tasks = visibleTasks.filter(t => t.status.key === status.key);
}
```

```js
// FIX — single pass groupBy
const byStatus = Object.groupBy(visibleTasks, t => t.status.key);
// or for older targets:
const byStatus = visibleTasks.reduce((acc, t) => {
  (acc[t.status.key] ??= []).push(t);
  return acc;
}, {});
for (const status of STATUSES) {
  const tasks = byStatus[status.key] ?? [];
}
```

**DOM query per status — `inline-dom.js:149`**

```js
// CURRENT — 5 querySelector calls per sync
for (const status of STATUSES) {
  const column = element.querySelector(`.task-kanban-inline-column[data-status-key="${status.key}"]`);
}
```

```js
// FIX — query once, index by key
const columns = Object.fromEntries(
  Array.from(element.querySelectorAll(".task-kanban-inline-column"))
    .map(el => [el.dataset.statusKey, el])
);
for (const status of STATUSES) {
  const column = columns[status.key];
}
```

**File read per kanban block — `workspace.js:37`**

If a file has 3 `task-kanban` blocks, file content is read and `scanTasksInContent()` called 3 times.

```js
// FIX — read once, pass to all blocks
const content = await this.app.vault.read(file);
const tasks = scanTasksInContent(content);
for (const element of elements) {
  await this.syncInlineKanbanDom(element, file, tasks); // pass pre-scanned tasks
}
```

---

**3 refresh cycles per checkbox click — `workspace.js:63`**

```
click → 120ms refresh
      → 650ms backup refresh  
      → 1200ms backup-backup refresh
```

All three run `syncInlineKanbanDom` (file read + task scan + innerHTML replace). The backups exist to handle editor debounce, but all three fire for every interaction.

```js
// FIX — single refresh with smarter invalidation flag
// If 120ms refresh succeeded (file was readable), cancel the 650ms/1200ms timers
async function doRefresh(file) {
  try {
    await syncInlineKanbanDom(...);
    clearPendingBackupTimers(file); // cancel 650ms + 1200ms if already succeeded
  } catch { /* leave backups in place */ }
}
```

**Filter UI rebuild on every sync — `inline-dom.js:198`**

`renderInlineHeadingFilter()` regenerates the entire filter menu `innerHTML` every sync, even when headings haven't changed.

```js
// FIX — track last rendered headings, skip if unchanged
const headings = Array.from(new Set(tasks.map(t => t.heading || "")));
const cacheKey = headings.join("\0");
if (element._lastHeadingFilterKey === cacheKey) return;
element._lastHeadingFilterKey = cacheKey;
menu.innerHTML = options.join("");
```

---

**Sort key recomputed O(n log n) times — `state.js:50`**

```js
// CURRENT — getTaskTouchedKey() calls hashString(), runs per comparator call
tasks.sort((a, b) => {
  const diff = (touchedAt[getTaskTouchedKey(b)] || 0)
             - (touchedAt[getTaskTouchedKey(a)] || 0);
});
```

```js
// FIX — precompute keys once before sort
const keyed = tasks.map(t => ({ task: t, key: getTaskTouchedKey(t) }));
keyed.sort((a, b) => (touchedAt[b.key] || 0) - (touchedAt[a.key] || 0));
const sorted = keyed.map(k => k.task);
```

**Text overflow detection reads layout on every sync — `inline-dom.js:69`**

`getComputedStyle(text).lineHeight` + `text.scrollHeight` forces layout for every card on every refresh.

```js
// FIX — cache per card element, invalidate on text change
function isTextOverflowing(text) {
  if (text._overflowChecked) return text._isOverflowing;
  const lineHeight = Number.parseFloat(getComputedStyle(text).lineHeight) || 18;
  text._overflowing = text.scrollHeight > lineHeight * 3 + 2;
  text._overflowChecked = true;
  return text._overflowing;
}
// Bust cache only when card is rebuilt (set _overflowChecked = false)
```

---

**`taskKanbanTouchedAt` grows unbounded — `state.js:42`**

Every task status change writes to this object. Tasks get deleted, but their keys remain. Persisted to disk — file size grows over time.

```js
// FIX — prune on load and periodically
function pruneTaskTouchedAt(touchedAt, activeTasks) {
  const activeKeys = new Set(activeTasks.map(t => getTaskTouchedKey(t)));
  for (const key of Object.keys(touchedAt)) {
    if (!activeKeys.has(key)) delete touchedAt[key];
  }
}
// Call after collectTasks() during plugin load and on vault.delete
```

**Event listeners bound without cleanup — `plugin.js:47-173`**

`registerMarkdownPostProcessor` binds drag/click listeners per element. If Obsidian re-renders the element (live preview refresh), old listeners stay attached.

```js
// FIX — use AbortController per element
const ac = new AbortController();
element._kanbabort = ac;
column.addEventListener("dragover", handler, { signal: ac.signal });
// On element removal or re-render:
element._kanbabort?.abort();
```

**`inlineKanbanExpandedBlockIds` accumulates stale block IDs — `state.js:88`**

Block IDs for deleted tasks are never removed. Minor but accumulates across sessions.

```js
// FIX — intersect with current task block IDs after scan
function pruneExpandedIds(expandedSet, currentTasks) {
  const validIds = new Set(currentTasks.flatMap(t =>
    [t.blockId, ...t.subtasks.map(s => s.blockId)].filter(Boolean)
  ));
  for (const id of expandedSet) {
    if (!validIds.has(id)) expandedSet.delete(id);
  }
}
```

---

**Double `requestAnimationFrame` scroll restore — `plugin.js:76`, `inline-status.js:35`, `inline-delegates.js:225`**

```js
// CURRENT — double-nested, adds ~16ms extra latency
window.requestAnimationFrame(() => window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {
  editor.scrollTo?.(saved.left, saved.top);
}));
```

Double rAF is a pattern to wait for a paint cycle, but here it's after `innerHTML` replacement which doesn't need two frames. Single rAF is sufficient:

```js
window.requestAnimationFrame(() => editor.scrollTo?.(saved.left, saved.top));
```

**Two-pass block ID scan — `block-ids.js:20-49`**

First pass collects existing IDs, second pass adds missing ones. Can be merged:

```js
// FIX — single pass: collect IDs + track which lines need them
const usedIds = new Set();
const needsId = [];
for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
  const id = lines[i].match(BLOCK_ID_RE)?.[1];
  if (id) usedIds.add(id);
  else if (isTaskLine(lines[i])) needsId.push(i);
}
for (const lineIdx of needsId) {
  lines[lineIdx] += " ^" + generateUniqueId(usedIds);
}
```

